  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kansas received $3.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $1.8B, the Department of Defense obligated $571M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $462M. Obligations fell 14.5% year over year. Agencies made 23,455 awards to Kansas vendors at an average award size of $131K. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. received $1.6B and is the largest vendor by obligations. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $1.6B, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounted for $380M. Historical obligations were $2.9B in FY21, $4.2B in FY22, $3B in FY23, $3.3B in FY24, $3.6B in FY25, and $3.1B in FY26 to date. The data shows concentration in health IT, defense-related manufacturing, and air transportation support, with the VA dominating buying in the state.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drove federal contract obligations in Kansas?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $1.8B, making the VA the largest buyer in Kansas. The Department of Defense obligated $571M and the Department of Transportation obligated $462M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $113M and the Environmental Protection Agency obligated $46.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captured the largest shares of federal dollars in Kansas?",
        "body": "ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. received $1.6B and is the largest vendor by obligations. INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. received $382M and ENVISION XPRESS INC received $96M. Computer Systems Design Services received $1.6B and Aircraft Manufacturing received $92.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
